    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-06T15:55:52+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-06T15:55:52+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-06T06:25:52Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-06T06:25:52Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A weak high pressure system centred over NSW will slowly move east while maintaining a ridge over SA until Saturday. A strong cold front will then begin to move into the Bight and move east over the state from late Saturday and throughout Sunday. Another cold front is then forecast to move into the Bight from late Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-06T15:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-07T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-06T05:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-06T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. Winds north to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending east to northeasterly in the evening.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-07T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-08T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-06T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-07T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west. Winds northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h turning northerly 25 to 35 km/h early in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to high 20s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:20am to 2:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-08T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-09T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-07T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-08T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of rain, most likely in the evening. Winds north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending west to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 25.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-09T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-10T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-08T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-09T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of rain east of Coober Pedy, high chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Stuart Highway in the afternoon. Winds west to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h tending west to southwesterly 35 to 55 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching around 16.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-10T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-11T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-09T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-10T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Woomera, near zero chance elsewhere. Areas of morning frost north of Coober Pedy. Winds westerly 20 to 30 km/h turning northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 2 and 6 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
